cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use bibr in research, please cite the software and report the version
  you used. When available, cite the DOI of that version's Zenodo archive.
type: software
title: "bibr: Scientific paper extraction to structured JSON"
authors:
  - family-names: Werner
    given-names: Jakub
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-09-12
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/scienceverse/bibr"
url: "https://bibr.org"
abstract: >-
  bibr extracts metadata, full text, references, tables, figures, and equations
  from scientific papers into structured JSON. It supports PDF, DOCX, JATS XML,
  HTML, and ePub, with native parsing, layout detection, selective OCR, and local
  or cloud extraction models. Sentence and page references help researchers
  check extractions against the source. Interfaces include Python, a command-line
  tool, an HTTP API, a web demo, and MCP.
keywords:
  - scientific document processing
  - metadata extraction
  - reference extraction
  - metascience
  - research software
